# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Prettier and the checks expect LF, and the shell scripts have to be LF to
# run in the Docker image. A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` on wrote
# CRLF into the working copy, and then `npm run format:check` flagged every
# file and a comment check read lines ending in `\r`. This wins over
# `core.autocrlf`, so the working copy is what the repository holds.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so no line ending is ever looked for in them. `text=auto` would
# usually tell; these say so rather than leave it to a guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.mp3 binary
*.m4a binary
*.opus binary
*.ogg binary
*.flac binary
*.wav binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.onnx binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
